apy referral . hey dragon , order an autoimmune profile . and then from a hypertension standpoint you , because your blood pressure is a little elevated today , i\'d like you to continue to monitor it at home and , you know , send me a report in the next couple of weeks sh- , you know , giving me the , the blood pressure reportings . do you have a blood pressure cuff at home ?\n[patient] yes , i do .\n[doctor] okay . and then , um , we\'ll go ahead and order a lipid profile for you . hey dragon , order a lipid profile . and then for , from a diabetes standpoint let\'s go ahead and , uh , continue you on your metformin 500 mg twice a day . okay ?\n[patient] okay .\n[doctor] do you have any questions ?\n[patient] no , that\'s it .\n[doctor] okay . the nurse will be in soon . it was good to see you .\n[patient] nice seeing you too .\n[doctor] hey dragon , finalize the note .\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nLeft knee pain.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nJanet Rodriguez is a 33-year-old female who presents today for the evaluation of left knee pain.\n\nThe onset of the patient\'s left knee pain began several months ago. The pain is bilateral and has been progressively worsening over time. She has been engaging in more stair workouts, which she thought would help build muscle on her knees, but it has only made the pain worse. The patient denies any other joint pain, except for her right shoulder, which she underwent a rotator cuff repair 2 years ago. She denies any numbness or tingling in her feet. She denies any swelling in her legs. She also reports that she has high blood pressure and diabetes, but her blood sugar has been under control. She denies fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, or shortness of breath.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies fever, chills, nausea, vomiting, chest pain, or shortness of breath.\nMusculoskeletal: Reports left knee pain. Denies right shoulder pain.\nEndocrine: Reports diabetes. Denies right shoulder pain.\nNeurological: Denies numbness or tingling in feet.\n\nVITALS\n\nBlood pressure is elevated today.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nNeck\n- General Examination: Neck is supple without any lymphadenopathy, thyromegaly, or bruits.\n\nRespiratory\n- Auscultation of Lungs: Clear bilaterally.\n\nCardiovascular\n- Auscultation of Heart: Regular rate and rhythm.\n\nGastrointestinal\n- Examination: Abdomen is soft and non-tender. No hepatosplenomegaly.\n\nMusculoskeletal\n- Examination of Knees: On the left knee, there is erythema and edema. There is a small effusion present over the left knee. She has a decrease in flexion and extension of the knee. Strength in the lower extremities is good.\n\nRESULTS\n\nX-rays of the left knee are unremarkable.\n\nLabs are within normal limits except for her HbA1c.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nJanet Rodriguez is a 33-year-old female who presents today for the evaluation of left knee pain. She has a past medical history significant for hypertension and diabetes. She also has a past surgical history significant for a right rotator cuff repair 2 years ago.\n\n1. Left knee pain.\n- Medical Reasoning: The patient\'s x-ray of the left knee is unremarkable. Her labs are within normal limits except for her HbA1c.\n- Diagnosis: Pain in the left knee.\n- Medical Treatment: We will order an autoimmune profile. We will refer her to physical therapy. We will also start her on meloxicam 15 mg once a day.\n\n2. Hypertension.\n- Medical Reasoning: Her blood pressure is elevated today.\n- Medical Treatment: We will continue her Norvasc 5 mg once a day. We will order a lipid profile.\n\n3. Diabetes.\n- Medical Reasoning: Her HbA1c is elevated.\n- Medical Treatment: We will continue her Metformin 500 mg twice a day.\n\nPLAN\n\nWe will order an autoimmune profile. We will refer her to physical therapy. We will start her on meloxicam 15 mg once a day. She will continue her Norvasc 5 mg once a day. We will order a lipid profile. We will continue her M