 okay . and when was your last pap smear ?\n[patient] uh , about six months ago . it came back normal , though .\n[doctor] okay . good , okay . well , let\'s see ... let\'s take a look at you , and then , we\'ll get some samples for std testing . okay ?\n[patient] all right .\n[doctor] you\'ll hear me talk through your exam , so that i can get it all documented . uh- ?\n[doctor] use my general physical exam template . pelvic exam demonstrates no external lesions . normal labia majora and labia minora . normal physiological discharge , with normal color and smell .\n[doctor] ms. ross , i\'m going to touch you , now . you\'ll feel my fingers , and the speculum in your vagina . you\'ll feel some pressure , now .\n[doctor] cervix is normal . vaginal wall is normal . no cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted . swabs were done for std testing .\n[doctor] okay , ms. ross . everything looks good from a visual standpoint . i\'m going to send off std testing for , uh , gonorrhea , chlamydia , trichomoniasis , and i\'ll have you give some blood for syphilis , hiv and hepatitis c. some of these tests will take longer than others . we will call you , if we see anything , but if you have n\'t heard anything , you can call us in three days for results .\n[patient] okay . sounds good . thank you , so much .\n[doctor] of course , my pleasure . and , if everything is normal , i\'ll see you again , at your next annual checkup .\n[doctor] assessment : is screen for std .\n[doctor] plan : discussed with patient , and please add that she is high risk due to an abnormal pap smear in the past , and the recent discovery of her sexual partner having multiple partners , for some period of time .\n[doctor] end of recording .\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ CHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nFull spectrum STD testing.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nGrace Ross is a 24-year-old female who presents today for a screening of all STDs. The patient reports that she has been experiencing symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in the vaginal region. She states that the right side of her vagina is starting to become painful. She denies fevers or chills. She reports that she recently learned that her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people and she wants to be evaluated for all STDs.\n\nThe patient states that she started noticing some abnormal discharge last week. She adds that it smells different and is not the same color or consistency as usual. She also reports that the right side of her vagina is sore. She denies that this ever phased her until she noticed the soreness on the right side of her vagina has not gone away.\n\nThe patient states that she has been dating her partner for three years. She notes that she has had an irregular pap smear in the past and has not had one since she was 20 years old. She also states that her last pap smear was about six months ago and it came back normal.\n\nMEDICAL HISTORY\n\nPatient reports that she has had an irregular pap smear in the past.\n\nSOCIAL HISTORY\n\nPatient reports that she is a college graduate and works as an administrative assistant. She reports that she is currently on summer break.\n\nFAMILY HISTORY\n\nPatient reports that her mother has diabetes.\n\nMEDICATIONS\n\nPatient reports that she does not have any current medications.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\nConstitutional: Denies fevers or chills.\nGynecologic: Reports abnormal discharge, soreness on the right side of the vagina, and odor in the vaginal region.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAM\n\nPelvic exam demonstrates no external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were done for std testing.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\n• Screening for STD.\n\nPLAN\n\nI discussed the importance of the std testing with the patient today. We discu